### [Component 2] Backend Database Allocation Schema & Controllers

We will define the database model and REST APIs to manage project allocations and student claiming.

#### [NEW] [CapstonePool.js](file:///c:/Users/vinay/Desktop/V2-Recalio/wemade_logix/mern/wemade_logix_mernstack/server/models/CapstonePool.js)
Define a MongoDB model storing:
* `projectCode` (String, e.g., `"FP-01"`, unique index)
* `title` (String, required)
* `assignedTo` (ObjectId, ref: `'User'`, default `null`)
* `assignedAt` (Date)

#### [NEW] [capstoneController.js](file:///c:/Users/vinay/Desktop/V2-Recalio/wemade_logix/mern/wemade_logix_mernstack/server/controllers/capstoneController.js)
Implement backend controllers:
* `getMyAssignedProject`: Resolves the logged-in student's project code. If not assigned, triggers atomic findOneAndUpdate to claim an unassigned code.
* `getAdminCapstones`: Populates and retrieves all 32 projects, joining student details and assignment submission status for allocated entries.
* `releaseCapstoneAllocation`: Releases a project code back into the pool (clears `assignedTo` field).
* `seedCapstonePool`: Seeds the 32 project documents on start if database is empty.

#### [NEW] [capstoneRoutes.js](file:///c:/Users/vinay/Desktop/V2-Recalio/wemade_logix/mern/wemade_logix_mernstack/server/routes/capstoneRoutes.js)
Map Express routes to the capstone controllers:
* `GET /api/capstone/my` (Student/Private)
* `GET /api/capstone/admin` (Admin/Private)
* `POST /api/capstone/admin/release` (Admin/Private)

#### [MODIFY] [index.js](file:///c:/Users/vinay/Desktop/V2-Recalio/wemade_logix/mern/wemade_logix_mernstack/server/index.js)
* Register `/api/capstone` route middleware linking to `capstoneRoutes.js`.
* Run `seedCapstonePool()` inside MongoDB connection then block.

